                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I found the concept very intresting, you choose between red, blue and green, (rock, paper and scissors) and you can hunt, be neutral or be hunted depending on the color you have activated and the color your opponents have.\n\nSadly by the time i got to test the game, there wasnt anyone playing online, so i only got to play the tutorial, and the \"Endurance\" mode, where you battle a bunch of AI shapes, the game is definitively meant to play with friends at least until more people play it.\n\nI didnt get to play all the levels, but they seemed all to be a big room with shapes placed around it, there are no \"corridors\" or really any hiding places.\n\nIt has controller support, i tried it out with my Xbox 360 controller and i didnt have to modify anything to use it, but there are no remappable keys on the gamepad or the kb+mouse.\n\nIt also has no mouse sensitivity or speed settings, no graphic options (not that they are really needed) maybe a brightness setting toogle, would be useful.\n\nThe movement is very fluid, the graphics are quite simple, so it doesnt look like it will be really demanding on any Pc.\n\nThe only thing \"bad\" i could find is the price, yes, i did get this for free from the Dev, but still, this game just has online matches i  and an endurance mode that doesnt really hold your intrest. (definitively feel it would be different with other players, or with bots maybe?) I think the game is a bit expensive at $8, maybe if some sort of Campaign was added the price would be justified.\n\nOverall i enjoyed it, liked the concept of rock, paper, scissors it just needs more players to be really enjoyable.",
